  "ingredients": [
    "2 (.25 ounce) packages active dry yeast",
    "3 tablespoons white sugar",
    "2.5 cups warm water (110 degrees F/45 degrees C)",
    "6.5 cups bread flour",
    "3 tablespoons lard, softened",
    "1 tablespoon salt"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/sWaleE6i0bpvJIc2_lvyc2BkAfI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-20066-traditional-white-bread-DDMFS-Step-1-83a584e582984257945fe945ac6ba742.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/20066/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dissolve yeast and sugar in warm water in a large bowl. Stir in 2 cups flour, lard, and salt. Stir in the remaining flour, 1/2 cup at a time, mixing well after each addition. When the dough comes together, turn it out onto a lightly floured surface and knead until smooth and elastic, about 8 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/S5-tsEWmFemQjuWGcDND0t-uA3Q=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-20066-traditional-white-bread-DDMFS-Step-3-98af84bbda4a4df5b0db0e30161cddd2.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/20066/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lightly oil a large bowl, then place the dough in the bowl and turn to coat with oil. Cover with a damp cloth and let rise in a warm place until doubled in volume, about 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/JHqMHdstwM3phy_PN1Eb8YJ1BjY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-20066-traditional-white-bread-DDMFS-Step-4-3595e83d12904fc6953401a349517489.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/20066/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lightly grease two 9x5-inch loaf pans.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/9QuuW4J0sdZJsXrBpHECxjBA2IU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-20066-traditional-white-bread-DDMFS-Step-5-77b8c984497b42b38a7e8e546f861d83.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/20066/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deflate the dough and turn it out onto a lightly floured surface. Divide the dough into two equal pieces and form into loaves. Place the loaves into the prepared pans, cover with a damp cloth, and let rise until doubled in volume, about 40 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/PZnEDtqBxfNr2VdIE4xHlBgk5TU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-20066-traditional-white-bread-DDMFS-Step-7-fb748e98dda04748b5cbe32243157f9c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/20066/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F (220 degrees C). Place bread in the preheated oven and lower the temperature to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Bake until the top is golden brown and the bottom of the loaf sounds hollow when tapped, about 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/nlrGnhHM6RNbAzahWafT0B-eGsI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-20066-traditional-white-bread-DDMFS-Step-8-59bc413e1fec441c84e5450556eb6bef.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/20066/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/FcoT_ZL76jZomB-qOBf8v5duZ5A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-20066-traditional-white-bread-DDMFS-4x3-f8e3aac2eee948dfacca38c877c59d14.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/20066/step_07.webp"
